# Code Review

Review against the spec folder (`spec.md`, `plan.md`, `tasks.md`) and `docs/CONSTITUTION.md` — not preference.

## Scope and evidence
- Is every changed file inside `plan.md`'s change surface (or is the extension recorded and re-confirmed)?
- Does each commit correspond to one task, with its test?
- Does `tasks.md` § Gate results show red-then-green evidence, and say what wasn't run?
- Does any change violate a constitution principle (authorization loosened, existing migration edited, types silenced, unjustified dependency)?

## Correctness
- Each acceptance criterion AND each requirement from every filled section (Security, Accessibility, Privacy, Performance, Observability, Deployment) is implemented
- Edge cases from the spec are handled; external data is validated at boundaries; errors are handled

## Doc accuracy
- Committed pre-implementable docs still match the implementation; divergences were reconciled in a `docs:` commit or called out in a task commit's body

## Conventions and quality
- Follows `AGENTS.md`, nested `AGENTS.md`, and existing patterns; no parallel way of doing something that already has a house pattern
- No silenced types; no premature abstraction; no speculative features; no commented-out code
- **Comments: almost none.** Flag comments that restate the code, repeat signatures, narrate steps, label sections, or record history; keep only one- or two-line notes of an invisible *why*

## Pull request
- The description matches the diff — no phantom changes, no omissions, honest "not verified" items

## Report format
- **[critical]** `file:line` — must fix before delivery
- **[warning]** `file:line` — should fix
- **[nit]** `file:line` — minor
End with approve / approve with nits / request changes, and what you did not review.
